<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10101" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντι-ληπτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντί-λᾱπτ-</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>able to apprehend,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ti.Locr.
					100c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρωμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Herc.</u>
					19.18
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναμις ἀ. πληγῆς ἀέρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.98b
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. δύναμις,</span> of the soul, <i><span class="en">
				Aristo Stoic.
				1.86
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				2.230
			</span></i>; <i>assisting</i> a scion <i>to unite,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλισχρότης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					1.6.4
				</span></i>
			; of the hand, <i>prehensile,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				2.6
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἔχειν</span> to be <i>aware,
				apprehend,</i> Hierocl.<i><span class="en">
				p.19A.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>taking hold of,</i> i.e. <i>impressing itself upon</i> the
			senses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					89.3
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Cass.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				35
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Comm.Math.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>able to check,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Def.</u>
				416a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>self-controlled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr</u>
				188
			</span></i>.</div>
